_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a category.\nThe <MATH_0002>-category of categories\nover <MATH_0003> has 2-fibre products.\nSuppose that\n<MATH_0004> and\n<MATH_0005> are morphisms of categories over\n<MATH_0006>.\nAn explicit 2-fibre product\n<MATH_0007> is given by the following\ndescription\n<STRUCT_0002>\n<STRUCT_0003> an object of <MATH_0008> is a quadruple\n<MATH_0009>, where <MATH_0010>,\n<MATH_0011>, <MATH_0012>,\nand <MATH_0013> is an isomorphism in <MATH_0014>,\n<STRUCT_0004> a morphism <MATH_0015> is given by a pair\n<MATH_0016>, where <MATH_0017> is a morphism in <MATH_0018>, and\n<MATH_0019> is a\nmorphism in <MATH_0020> such that\n<STRUCT_0005>\n<STRUCT_0006> <MATH_0021> and <MATH_0022> induce the same morphism <MATH_0023>, and\n<STRUCT_0007> the diagram\n<MATH_0024>\nis commutative.\n<STRUCT_0008>\n<STRUCT_0009>\nThe functors <MATH_0025>\nand <MATH_0026> are the\nforgetful functors in this case. The transformation <MATH_0027> is given on the object <MATH_0028> by\n<MATH_0029>.\n<STRUCT_0010>", "source_text_hash": "sha256:7891914cbc58fa48287dc991a25a8060895716462ef47fafa79e6db5c37c44af", "unit_id": "inventory:categories:0040:lemma/0001"}, "state": "READY"}}, "model_output": {"hash": "sha256:94dadd8224893ee6637bb32250ff41cf20246a5de025f6bfe89ead5c6afc30d9", "path": "docs/evidence/categories-completion-p016-raw.jsonl", "record_hash": "sha256:35fddd9855068c7a45ffbf3ed269ac201a0f7472f603940aaab64ea38c2e4d7f"}, "neighbor_unit_ids": ["tag:0047:proof"], "policy_revision": "git:e7a1627e7bce13592b8c07d43974a815ba27c0d5", "prompt_version": "translator-v2", "read_context": {"citations": [], "neighbors": [{"context_id": "inventory:categories:0042:paragraph/0003", "relation": "before"}, {"context_id": "inventory:categories:0047:proof/0001", "relation": "after"}], "references": [{"context_id": "reference:categories-lemma-2-product-categories-over-C", "label": "lemma-2-product-categories-over-C"}], "unit_id": "tag:0047:statement"}, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a87